course: dictionary
lesson: 8693
title: Selection and choosing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Selection means choosing someone or something from a group. It can also mean the set of things that have been chosen, or a range of things you can pick from. «A wide selection» tells you there are lots of things to choose from.
explain: The word often shows up in a phrase. «A selection of cakes» means several cakes that someone has picked out. «Team selection» means the choosing of players for a team. The clue is in the words next to it, so read the whole phrase.
explain: In science, natural selection is a special meaning. «Natural selection, the idea of Charles Darwin and Alfred Russel Wallace» describes how living things that suit their surroundings survive and have young. Whenever you meet a new word, check the words around it to find the meaning.
fact: Selection means choosing someone or something from a group.
fact: A selection can also be a set of things that have been chosen, or a range of things to choose from.
fact: «Natural selection» is how living things that suit their surroundings survive and have young.
fact: In computing, a selection is the part of the screen that has been highlighted.
exercise: «The shop has a wide selection of cakes.» What does selection mean here? | Cakes that are burnt | *A range of things to choose from | A shop that is closed | A type of cake recipe
exercise: Mia waited nervously for team selection. What is team selection? | *The choosing of players for a team | A team that has lost its match | The team's new kit | Training in the park
exercise: Natural selection is how living things that suit their surroundings survive and have young. Which living things survive? | Those that are kept as pets only | *Those that suit their surroundings | Those that are the biggest in the world | Those that never move
test: «Birds ate the stick insects that looked least like twigs, so over many generations the survivors looked more and more like twigs.» What is this an example of? | Team selection | *Natural selection | A selection box of sweets | A wide selection of cakes
test: «People choosing which dogs had puppies made chihuahuas and Great Danes.» What kind of selection is this, where people do the choosing? | Natural selection | A selection of toys | *Artificial selection | Team selection
exam: In the phrase «a wide selection», what does selection mean? | The highlighted part of a screen | *A set of things to choose from | A small box of sweets | Choosing a team captain from a group
